---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Contact — Noven';
const description =
  'Book Noven’s £30 audit or ask a question. Email us your business name, website and the services you want to be found for, and we’ll reply within two working days.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Book the audit, or just ask</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The simplest way to reach us is email. No forms, no call-booking software, no follow-up
        sequence — you'll get a reply from a person.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>How do I book the £30 audit?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Email us with four things:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your business name</li>
          <li>Your website address</li>
          <li>The services you most want to be found for</li>
          <li>The area you serve</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We'll reply within two working days to confirm scope and payment, and you'll have your
          written report within one working day of that.
        </p>
        <ul class="contact-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Email:</strong>
            <a href="mailto:hello.noven.uk@gmail.com">hello.noven.uk@gmail.com</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Based in:</strong> the Wirral — working with clients across the UK
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We don't publish a phone number. Everything here starts by email, so there's a written
          record of what was asked and what we said — and you're not chasing anyone to pick up.
          If a call would be easier once we're working together, we'll arrange one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Not ready to book?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          That's fine — this is a considered purchase and we'd rather you read first. The
          <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a> page explains each stage, the
          <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> has every number, and the
          <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> answers the sceptical questions, including "why should I trust a
          company with no case studies?"
        </p>
        <p>
          If you'd rather just ask something directly, email is fine for that too. Short questions
          get short answers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
